            <td class="text-right">82.8%</td>
            <td class="text-right">16.6%</td>
            <td class="text-right">0.7%</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SECTION 2: PRICING ANALYSIS -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-number">2</div>
      <h2>Pricing Dynamics Across Cities</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">Comparing median and average nightly prices by city and room type, identifying the most and least expensive markets, and highlighting price dispersion within each city.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="chart-container-wide">
      <div class="chart-title">Median Nightly Price by City (USD) — Cities with Available Price Data</div>
      <canvas id="priceBarChart"></canvas>
      <div class="color-legend">
        <span><span class="color-dot" style="background:#2563eb;"></span> Median price (USD)</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: 8px;" class="data-note">
      Bangkok's median price ($1,400) is more than 6× higher than other cities in the dataset. This likely reflects a currency normalization issue in the source data — prices for Bangkok appear to be in Thai Baht rather than USD (1,400 THB ≈ $40 USD), suggesting the dataset mixes unconverted local currencies for this market. Treat Bangkok pricing comparisons with caution.
    </div>

    <div class="chart-row" style="margin-top: 28px;">
      <div class="chart-container">
        <div class="chart-title">Median Price by Room Type (USD)</div>
        <canvas id="roomTypeChart"></canvas>
        <div class="color-legend">
